---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../../components/PhotoPlaceholder.astro'

const title = 'Wearside Golf Club — Pin High Media'
const description = 'How Pin High built Wearside Golf Club a new website and a full suite of bespoke tools — course status, halfway house ordering, table booking, and open competition scoring.'

const products = ['ClubSentinel', 'Integrated Website']
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>

  <section class="ph-page-head">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <div class="ph-back"><a href="/case-studies">← All case studies</a></div>
      <h1 class="ph-page-h1">Wearside Golf Club</h1>
      <p class="ph-page-lede">
        A club website and suite of tools, built from scratch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="ph-container">
      <div class="ph-case-detail-art">
        <PhotoPlaceholder kind="course" ratio="21/9" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-case-detail-body">
    <div class="ph-container ph-case-detail-grid">
      <div>
        <p>
          Like most golf clubs, Wearside's digital setup was built around administration software — competition management, bar systems, membership records. The website was an afterthought. Bundled in with a legacy platform, unsupported, and lacking the kind of features members at any modern organisation would take for granted. No video. No proper hero. No dynamic content.
        </p>
        <p>
          Replacing it wasn't just a case of building a new site. The legacy system handled things like course status updates automatically — so before I could switch anything over, I needed to build the tools to replace that functionality first.
        </p>
        <p>
          So that's what I did.
        </p>
        <p>
          The course status tool lets the greenkeeper update conditions directly — no technical knowledge needed. An admin tool handles open competition scores. The halfway house ordering system lets members scan a QR code on the eighth tee and place their food order for collection — ready and waiting by the time they walk in. And a table booking system for the bar and kitchen links directly into a single booking admin, giving staff a complete view of both halfway house orders and table reservations in one place.
        </p>
        <p>
          These aren't features you'd expect at Wearside. These are features you'd expect at a multi-million pound club, if you'd expect them anywhere at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          Wearside now has them.
        </p>

        <ul class="ph-case-detail-list">
          {products.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-closing">
    <div class="ph-closing-inner">
      <h2 class="ph-closing-h">Software that understands golf.</h2>
      <p class="ph-closing-p">Tell us what your club, county, or tour is wrestling with — we probably know the problem already.</p>
      <div class="ph-hero-ctas ph-closing-ctas">
        <a href="/contact" class="ph-btn ph-btn-primary">
          Get in touch
          <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 6h8m-3-3 3 3-3 3"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/case-studies" class="ph-btn ph-btn-ghost">
          All case studies
          <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 6h8m-3-3 3 3-3 3"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
